# Needed Test Cases
!! > SEE FUTURE_DEV punto 10 
## System

- [x] Verify application context starts with default test profile.
- [x] Verify core controllers are registered in the Spring context.
- [x] Verify auth controller routes are reachable through Spring MVC routing.
- [x] Verify every controller route is reachable through Spring MVC routing.
- [x] Verify global error response shape for validation, not found, conflict, unauthorized, and forbidden errors.
- [x] Verify OpenAPI/Swagger endpoint starts and includes secured endpoints.
- [x] Verify database migrations/schema creation work for test and dev profiles.
- [x] Verify fake external clients are active in dev/test profiles and real clients are not used accidentally.
- [x] Verify endpoint coverage tracking records controller routes.
- [x] Verify health/basic startup behavior with empty database.

## Auth

- [x] Register user with valid email/password returns JWT and normalized email.
- [x] Register rejects duplicate email case-insensitively.
- [x] Register rejects invalid email and short password.
- [x] Register rejects blank fields and malformed JSON.
- [x] Login returns JWT for valid credentials.
- [x] Login accepts email with different case.
- [x] Login rejects wrong password.
- [x] Login rejects unknown email.
- [x] Current-user endpoint returns authenticated user data.
- [x] Protected endpoints reject missing token.
- [x] Protected endpoints reject malformed token.
- [x] Protected endpoints reject expired/invalid-signature token.
- [x] Auth response never exposes password hash.

## Roles

- [x] `USER` cannot create hackathons.
- [x] `ORGANIZER` can create and manage own hackathons.
- [x] Non-organizer cannot add mentors or judges.
- [x] Organizer cannot assign a user as mentor unless user role is `MENTOR`.
- [x] Organizer cannot assign a user as judge unless user role is `JUDGE`.
- [x] Mentor can view support requests for assigned hackathons.
- [x] Mentor is denied support requests for unassigned hackathons.
- [x] Judge can evaluate submissions only for assigned hackathons.
- [x] Judge can view submissions only for assigned hackathons.
- [x] User cannot view staff-only submission/evaluation/report endpoints.
- [x] Organizer can view registrations, reports, submissions, and evaluations for own hackathon.
- [x] Cross-hackathon staff access is denied.

## Lifecycle

- [x] Hackathon starts in `REGISTRATION_OPEN` after creation.
- [x] Reject invalid date ordering during hackathon creation.
- [x] Allow valid status transition `REGISTRATION_OPEN` -> `IN_PROGRESS`.
- [x] Allow valid status transition `IN_PROGRESS` -> `EVALUATION`.
- [x] Allow valid status transition `EVALUATION` -> `FINISHED`.
- [x] Reject invalid status transitions.
- [ ] Reject registration after registration deadline.
- [ ] Reject submission before submission phase.
- [x] Reject submission after submission deadline.
- [ ] Reject evaluation before evaluation phase.
- [ ] Reject winner declaration before evaluation phase.
- [x] Reject winner declaration if any submission is unevaluated.
- [ ] Reject winner declaration if winner team has no submission.
- [x] Mark hackathon `FINISHED` after declaring winner.
- [ ] Prevent declaring winner twice.

## Flow

- [x] Full happy path: register, login, create hackathon, create team, invite member, accept invite, register team, submit, evaluate, declare winner.
- [ ] Invite flow rejects non-team-member inviter.
- [ ] Invite flow rejects inviting user already on a team.
- [ ] Invite flow rejects duplicate invitation.
- [x] Invitee can accept pending invitation.
- [x] Invitee can decline pending invitation.
- [ ] Non-invitee cannot accept/decline invitation.
- [ ] Accepted/declined invitation cannot be answered again.
- [x] Team registration works for a current team member.
- [ ] Team registration rejects current user who is not a team member.
- [ ] Team registration rejects already registered team.
- [ ] Team registration rejects team over max size.
- [x] Submission upsert creates new submission.
- [ ] Submission upsert updates existing submission.
- [x] My-team submission endpoint returns current team submission.
- [x] Support request creation requires hackathon in progress.
- [x] Support request creation requires registered team member.
- [x] Mentor call proposal marks support request as call proposed and stores external booking data.
- [x] Rule violation report can be created by a mentor with access.
- [ ] Rule violation report rejects mentor without access.
- [ ] Rule violation report rejects unregistered reported team.
- [x] Organizer can list rule violation reports.
- [x] Payment transaction is created when winner is declared.

## Service Unit Tests

- [x] Team creation adds creator as first member.
- [x] Team creation rejects user already in a team.
- [x] Submission listing rejects unassigned staff.
- [x] Evaluation creates a new evaluation when one does not exist.
- [x] Evaluation updates an existing evaluation.
- [x] Payment prize stores `COMPLETED` when the payment client succeeds.
- [x] Payment prize stores `FAILED` when the payment client fails.

